1ea45f86e0c6c7e76939408f1de62fe7ef3d104","sha":"71ea45f86e0c6c7e76939408f1de62fe7ef3d104","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/engage-chat/mattermost/commits/71ea45f86e0c6c7e76939408f1de62fe7ef3d104"}],"sha":"87d053d7f3f31e4ec12316f94c7011ea0368199a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/engage-chat/mattermost/commits/87d053d7f3f31e4ec12316f94c7011ea0368199a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/812088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fmartingr","id":812088,"login":"fmartingr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMjA4OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fmartingr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/engage-chat/mattermost/commits/71ea45f86e0c6c7e76939408f1de62fe7ef3d104/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T12:45:53Z","email":"812088+fmartingr@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Felipe Martin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T12:45:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Stop leaking message body via the Notifications API tag (#36364) (#37942)\n\n* Stop leaking message body via the Notifications API tag\n\nshowNotification was passing the rendered chat body as the Web Notifications\nAPI tag option. On Chromium-based browsers (Chrome, Edge, Brave), the tag is\nserialised into the notification-activation command line via the\n--notification-launch-id argument, where endpoint detection tooling such as\nCrowdStrike Falcon FDR, Microsoft Defender for Endpoint, and Sysmon Event ID 1\ncaptures the full process-start command line and forwards it to the customer''s\nSIEM. That meant private message content (including incident-response messages,\ncredentials accidentally pasted into chat, and customer PII) was being copied\ninto telemetry pipelines that were never in scope to receive it.\n\nUse the title - which already carries only the sender / channel context - as\nthe tag instead. As a side benefit this is closer to the spec-intended use of\ntag: subsequent notifications from the same conversation now replace the prior\none rather than stacking.\n\nAdd a regression test covering the leak: the test pushes a body with a\nplausible secret pattern (token=AKIA-...) and asserts the tag never echoes\nany of it.\n\n\n\n* Allow callers to pass an explicit notification tag\n\nThreads channelId through dispatchNotification so per-conversation\nnotifications coalesce by a stable opaque id rather than the user-visible\ntitle. The title remains as a safe fallback when callers do not supply a\ntag, preserving the existing behaviour for the session-expired notification\nemitted from login.tsx where no channel context exists.\n\n\n\n* fix: explain desktop notification path\n\n* Avoid title fallback for notification tags\n\n\n\n* test: align notification action payload expectations\n\n\n\n* test: align notification tag e2e expectation\n\n---------\n\n\n\n(cherry picked from commit befdb0175a882cecb722cc03d961044ddfe489c0)\n\nSigned-off-by: Vishal Kumar Singh <vishal.kr.singh2021@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Vishal Kumar Singh <vishal.kr.singh2021@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"36d7768dc238bf18796a8337bfffd32fc4b8e0c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/engage-chat/mattermost/git/trees/36d7768dc238bf18796a8337bfffd32fc4b8e0c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/engage-chat/mattermost/git/commits/71ea45f86e0c6c7e76939408f1de62fe7ef3d104","verification":{"payload":"tree 36d7768dc238bf18796a8337bfffd32fc4b8e0c3\nparent 073806337fa15aff191f777fb02ada280b3eb477\nauthor Felipe Martin <812088+fmartingr@users.noreply.github.com> 1786625153 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786625153 +0200\n\nStop leaking message body via the Notifications API tag (#36364) (#37942)\n\n* Stop leaking message body via the Notifications API tag\n\nshowNotification was passing the rendered chat body as the Web Notifications\nAPI tag option. On Chromium-based browsers (Chrome, Edge, Brave), the tag is\nserialised into the notification-activation command line via the\n--notification-launch-id argument, where endpoint detection tooling such as\nCrowdStrike Falcon FDR, Microsoft Defender for Endpoint, and Sysmon Event ID 1\ncaptures the full process-start command line and forwards it to the customer''s\nSIEM. That meant private message content (including incident-response messages,\ncredentials accidentally pasted into chat, and customer PII) was being copied\ninto telemetry pipelines that were never in scope to receive it.\n\nUse the title - which already carries only the sender / channel context - as\nthe tag instead. As a side benefit this is closer to the spec-intended use of\ntag: subsequent notifications from the same conversation now replace the prior\none rather than stacking.\n\nAdd a regression test covering the leak: the test pushes a body with a\nplausible secret pattern (token=AKIA-...) and asserts the tag never echoes\nany of it.\n\n\n\n* Allow callers to pass an explicit notification tag\n\nThreads channelId through dispatchNotification so per-conversation\nnotifications coalesce by a stable opaque id rather than the user-visible\ntitle. The title remains as a safe fallback when callers do not supply a\ntag, preserving the existing behaviour for the session-expired notification\nemitted from login.tsx where no channel context exists.\n\n\n\n* fix: explain desktop notification path\n\n* Avoid title fallback for notification tags\n\n\n\n* test: align notification action payload expectations\n\n\n\n* test: align notification tag e2e expectation\n\n---------\n\n\n\n(cherry picked from commit befdb0175a882cecb722cc03d961044ddfe489c0)\n\nSigned-off-by: Vishal Kumar Singh <vishal.kr.singh2021@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Vishal Kumar Singh <vishal.kr.singh2021@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfbyBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkBUQACH2HIuy82ViG7fchB8vR/I3\ns3YOkI69pw74Up21tx2MGAozpt7io++KBVMdsTrfuFa36af3QycnE7EwNy5rzLL8\n7WWtDNN1Ib2jSWYC9uEmOZ7RtEogkDNa2CgOJg+/MQ7BOyVTADg9CTfXPDcQkug7\neoWLexqBpJxWOB8/4P/cmVQ6XeO1UxVb1rhWzEnMveS548OXwY2OLI+/9uvhnyeE\nXs5zApyIr9H8N9eL4WZVUUKZ641apNVba2CsS9HHfJ34u4XmwqH6S7sqIRigk1mZ\naao3G9qqLuWChk73xAIqtjvheKZAaT4kM5uMLu/DaXB9oZaBW5OKLPBO9rHAI7YS\nhxbSc2rsK6a57l1psdq22zkuIRVn9KNDQ74FyV0exsrnVQKhZcqmTjISucNHmrjR\nbnqovgcodo8WPiV8LFD9l78hMUHkF9Rak+o9nSgmCiS4dEFTWla0P6fxKcmqoy5c\nt/39kXHuPXNluLx0pN1VaQvwetQKLWF5XlOJBuyjMElPcgg+b0U7Gi4e1IusBoOz\n0Pvut3x64amp6V+ssFqayiR1k6+hYXyW+c9LHes0fVmAzqwLvpWgu2BaOma3I8bt\ncMT+8gVtRJ1gyGFuFSbO52kdcwLCKVtU3tCseJ2IfeGR+6m/1uEAUOmiw/bBT3JN\nVL27iIB4/A1nG5f5eppM\n=HzYr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T10:39:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/