llowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattermost-build/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattermost-build/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattermost-build/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mattermost-build","id":10821961,"login":"mattermost-build","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODIxOTYx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattermost-build/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattermost-build/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattermost-build/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattermost-build/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattermost-build/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattermost-build","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/engage-chat/mattermost/commits/d42004bb3046de3ed176938a34b1a70c1c3d9421/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T08:49:50Z","email":"build@mattermost.com","name":"Mattermost Build"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T08:49:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: bot import panic when user exists without bot record (#36072) (#37785)\n\n* Fix bot import panic when user exists without bot record\n\nThe original importBot error handler re-declared `var appErr *model.AppError`\ninside the CreateBot failure block, shadowing the outer appErr with a typed nil\npointer. When errors.As received this (*model.AppError)(nil), it was a non-nil\ninterface — so instead of returning false, it called AppError.Unwrap() on the\nnil receiver, causing a panic.\n\nThis commit:\n- Fixes the variable shadowing that caused the panic\n- Adds recovery logic: when CreateBot fails because the username is taken,\n  look up the existing user and create/update just the bot record\n- Fixes pre-existing silent error swallowing in Bot().GetByUsername — now\n  distinguishes store.ErrNotFound from real database errors\n- Fixes pre-existing bug where DisplayName changes on re-import were lost\n  because DisplayName is stored in Users.FirstName, not the Bots table\n- Adds logging at every step of the recovery path (Info for normal flow,\n  Warn for fallback/error paths)\n- Uses distinct variable names (saveErr/updateErr) in the Save→Update\n  fallback to avoid the same class of variable-reuse hazard\n- Adds comprehensive test suite (11 subtests) covering dry-run, apply,\n  re-import, recovery, regression/panic guard, idempotency, DisplayName\n  update, and plugin-owner edge cases\n\n* Address review findings: tighten assertions, fix error ID, add coverage\n\n- Use require.ErrorAs for store.ErrNotFound instead of generic require.Error\n  in the dry-run test, so it catches only not-found rather than any store error\n- Add time.Sleep before idempotent re-import to ensure any real write would\n  produce a different UpdateAt timestamp at millisecond resolution\n- Fix misleading error ID \"app.bot.createbot.internal_error\" to\n  \"app.bot.update.internal_error\" in the Update fallback path\n- Add test for non-username CreateBot failure (email conflict) to cover\n  the error passthrough at line 907-908\n\n* Add missing i18n translations for bot import error strings\n\nAdd translation entries for app.bot.update.internal_error,\napp.import.import_bot.lookup_error, and\napp.import.import_bot.user_not_found.error to fix enterprise CI\ni18n check failure.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 694e6f40dcda8ac682a8f7d24e50cad3565078fa)\n\nCo-authored-by: Felipe Martin <812088+fmartingr@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b3065e6b3ae10610c145561010eaf29e2c101bfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/engage-chat/mattermost/git/trees/b3065e6b3ae10610c145561010eaf29e2c101bfa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/engage-chat/mattermost/git/commits/d42004bb3046de3ed176938a34b1a70c1c3d9421","verification":{"payload":"tree b3065e6b3ae10610c145561010eaf29e2c101bfa\nparent f52a22d0cf099ba25f8d508f9368f9317ad11e55\nauthor Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com> 1785487790 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785487790 +0200\n\nfix: bot import panic when user exists without bot record (#36072) (#37785)\n\n* Fix bot import panic when user exists without bot record\n\nThe original importBot error handler re-declared `var appErr *model.AppError`\ninside the CreateBot failure block, shadowing the outer appErr with a typed nil\npointer. When errors.As received this (*model.AppError)(nil), it was a non-nil\ninterface — so instead of returning false, it called AppError.Unwrap() on the\nnil receiver, causing a panic.\n\nThis commit:\n- Fixes the variable shadowing that caused the panic\n- Adds recovery logic: when CreateBot fails because the username is taken,\n  look up the existing user and create/update just the bot record\n- Fixes pre-existing silent error swallowing in Bot().GetByUsername — now\n  distinguishes store.ErrNotFound from real database errors\n- Fixes pre-existing bug where DisplayName changes on re-import were lost\n  because DisplayName is stored in Users.FirstName, not the Bots table\n- Adds logging at every step of the recovery path (Info for normal flow,\n  Warn for fallback/error paths)\n- Uses distinct variable names (saveErr/updateErr) in the Save→Update\n  fallback to avoid the same class of variable-reuse hazard\n- Adds comprehensive test suite (11 subtests) covering dry-run, apply,\n  re-import, recovery, regression/panic guard, idempotency, DisplayName\n  update, and plugin-owner edge cases\n\n* Address review findings: tighten assertions, fix error ID, add coverage\n\n- Use require.ErrorAs for store.ErrNotFound instead of generic require.Error\n  in the dry-run test, so it catches only not-found rather than any store error\n- Add time.Sleep before idempotent re-import to ensure any real write would\n  produce a different UpdateAt timestamp at millisecond resolution\n- Fix misleading error ID \"app.bot.createbot.internal_error\" to\n  \"app.bot.update.internal_error\" in the Update fallback path\n- Add test for non-username CreateBot failure (email conflict) to cover\n  the error passthrough at line 907-908\n\n* Add missing i18n translations for bot import error strings\n\nAdd translation entries for app.bot.update.internal_error,\napp.import.import_bot.lookup_error, and\napp.import.import_bot.user_not_found.error to fix enterprise CI\ni18n check failure.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 694e6f40dcda8ac682a8f7d24e50cad3565078fa)\n\nCo-authored-by: Felipe Martin <812088+fmartingr@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbGGuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgkwQAHWWum1kOu6N/v1hDMXc4pUM\ngjk8VDlyfPiIbk2NrTtaP0uyeUq0Y8ctgmm0LkS38CYr77cIttG8FUFdnU/dbjjq\nZTlzPt5VbPSEQ8NcY83qHmbEp2Al/GlurwdZgJNKnirAbD1Jyl4hWxl04y2vFVi/\np6muRZNAKhb0aoo7XcnoC/7ZDkHjywQZvxiErtm/nR8WQpD93RLL/6G6ivoPhmyY\nZlIVYZW1Y+WXzARMvS/4pv93ykUgaPCojrP73arpqCiHShO8ufIPMl1uMAa4XG2n\n/lx60Ep5VGGV1iUAw71BEdMh6U2UiHZi6Ccj/BXitYaD9jiBSNSDZeL2eKM6Z6kO\n3vQL4Z866id89Fu/MkMhy5WhOTvMz8B10Hh2UxbNCX3kpBe7ffO1Cwo/3a+jviFD\nHV3GF07GRuexru2t+M+6leE2YFyDwTmkRL0vt/9JTzh+pKSW8csLRvR7wcMo8GtD\nVj9YNLT6QWaYkqW/afu4LId2WRYOpDfQ5TRjFW+gVX3RtS+yAEGR9yJLAuxw4wJS\n2rCVeU1rqKqE+O5V9jWias3oqke7vXTXip+Orm4E99msdXvwRlWDQSh9ED+6NQli\nv/X+q2/aiOolBjygHHxu1oM0Bfxz+oYpjqEK/L7sYl1nQs6n+9egS7jWI+cWRzLB\n2Bbc73ZH9nzI64ME8c57\n=Rs2X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T10:39:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/engage-chat/mattermost/commit/d42004bb3046de3ed176938a34b1a70c1c3d9421","node_id":"C_kwDOPKK3K9oAKGQ0MjAwNGJiMzA0NmRlM2VkMTc2OTM4YTM0YjFhNzBjMWMzZDk0MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/engage-chat/mattermost/commit/f52a22d0cf099ba25f8d508f9368f9317ad11e55","sha":"f52a22d0cf099ba25f8d508f9368f9317ad11e55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/engage-chat/mattermost/commits/f52a22d0cf099ba25f8d508f9368f9317ad11e55"}],"sha":"d42004bb3046de3ed176938a34b1a70c1c3d9421","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/engage-chat/mattermost/commits/d42004bb3046de3ed176938a34b1a70c1c3d9421"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10082627?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pvev","id":10082627,"login":"pvev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDgyNjI3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pvev","user_view_type