"id":44273333,"login":"jslitzkerttcu","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjczMzMz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jslitzkerttcu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jslitzkerttcu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jslitzkerttcu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jslitzkerttcu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jslitzkerttcu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jslitzkerttcu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jslitzker/forgeboard/commits/5c535520525d7a1972184470cd73164819400962/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-07-14T17:06:04Z","email":"jslitzker@ttcu.com","name":"Joe Slitzker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-07-14T17:06:04Z","email":"jslitzker@ttcu.com","name":"Joe Slitzker"},"message":"fix: resolve authentication JSON parsing error and React Hooks violations\n\n- Fixed SSL module naming conflict that was breaking Python''s built-in ssl import\n- Renamed backend/ssl to backend/ssl_management to avoid module conflicts\n- Updated all import references to use ssl_management.manager\n- Added migration system for password_change_required field\n- Fixed React Hooks order violation in App.jsx by moving all useEffect calls before conditional returns\n- Updated SchemaMigration model to properly set applied_at timestamp\n- Fixed authentication flow with proper database migration (version 3)\n- Verified API proxy configuration is working correctly\n- Authentication endpoints now return proper JSON responses\n\nThe JSON parsing error was caused by the SSL module naming conflict preventing the backend from starting properly. The React Hooks error was preventing proper authentication state management in the frontend.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8e75ae94c8ac117890d916a16e4b7fe